{
 "id": "questions-negation",
 "title": "Poser des questions et nier",
 "level": "A1",
 "topic": "Grammaire",
 "summary": "L'ordre des mots d'une question, les mots interrogatifs, et les formes négatives de tous les temps.",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "L'ordre d'une question"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Schéma général : **mot interrogatif + auxiliaire + sujet + verbe**. L'auxiliaire dépend du temps : *do/does/did, am/is/are, have/has, will, can…*"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "head": [
    "Temps",
    "Question",
    "Négation"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "be",
     "Is she here?",
     "She isn't here."
    ],
    [
     "présent simple",
     "Do you work?",
     "I don't work."
    ],
    [
     "prétérit",
     "Did he call?",
     "He didn't call."
    ],
    [
     "present perfect",
     "Have you finished?",
     "I haven't finished."
    ],
    [
     "futur",
     "Will they come?",
     "They won't come."
    ],
    [
     "modal",
     "Can you help?",
     "I can't help."
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Les mots interrogatifs"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "head": [
    "Mot",
    "Sens",
    "Exemple"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "what",
     "quoi / quel",
     "What do you need?"
    ],
    [
     "where",
     "où",
     "Where does she live?"
    ],
    [
     "when",
     "quand",
     "When did it happen?"
    ],
    [
     "why",
     "pourquoi",
     "Why are you late?"
    ],
    [
     "who",
     "qui",
     "Who called you?"
    ],
    [
     "how",
     "comment",
     "How does it work?"
    ],
    [
     "how many / how much",
     "combien",
     "How many servers do you have?"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Sujet de la question : pas d'auxiliaire !"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Quand le mot interrogatif **est le sujet** (who, what), on n'utilise pas do/does/did : *Who **wrote** this?* — *What **happened**?*"
  },
  {
   "type": "h",
   "text": "Les question tags"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Petit morceau en fin de phrase pour demander confirmation : phrase positive → tag négatif, et inversement. *You like tea, **don't you**?* — *She isn't here, **is she**?*"
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "Where do you work?",
   "fr": "Où travailles-tu ?"
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "Why didn't you call me?",
   "fr": "Pourquoi ne m'as-tu pas appelé ?"
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "Who is coming tonight?",
   "fr": "Qui vient ce soir ?"
  },
  {
   "type": "ex",
   "en": "How much does it cost?",
   "fr": "Combien ça coûte ?"
  },
  {
   "type": "tip",
   "text": "**Piège** : *How many* + pluriel dénombrable, *how much* + indénombrable. *How much water? How many bottles?*"
  }
 ],
